    [Performance][MoE] Optimize NPU event recording for MoE multistream overlap (#17603)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The NPU events recorded around the routed-experts path (router
    milestones `shared_input_ready`/`router_output_ready`, and
    `before_dispatch`/`before_gmm2`/`before_combine` inside the routed path)
    are consumed **only** by the shared-expert side stream, which exists
    solely when `multistream_overlap_shared_expert` is enabled. When the
    overlap is off, every `record_event` is pure host-side overhead paid per
    MoE layer per step, and host-side record is notably slow.
    
    The consumers in `shared_experts.py` already gate every wait on the same
    flag (`_wait_for_milestone` returns immediately when the overlap is off
    and fails fast if a milestone is missing while it is on), and the
    `RoutedMoEMilestones`/`FusedExpertsResult` event fields are already
    `Optional`. So the producer-side records can be skipped safely with no
    consumer changes.
    
    This PR gates the always-on-path record sites behind the flag via a
    shared helper, `maybe_record_event()` (defined in
    `ops/fused_moe/moe_mlp.py`):
    
    - `ops/fused_moe/moe_mlp.py`: define `maybe_record_event()` and use it
    for the `before_gmm2_evt` record in `apply_moe_mlp`; the entry now
    returns an Optional event;
    - `ops/fused_moe/moe_comm_method.py`: gate `before_dispatch_evt` /
    `before_combine_evt`;
    - `ops/fused_moe/fused_moe.py`: gate `shared_input_ready` /
    `router_output_ready` in `_prepare_router_and_milestones`
    (`routed_finalize_done` is already recorded only on the SP-overlap
    gather path, so it needs no extra gating).
    
    `maybe_record_event()` skips the record only when the initialized config
    proves the overlap is off; an uninitialized config keeps the legacy
    always-record behavior. The 310P-specific and LoRA gmm2 records are
    intentionally left unconditional for now (not yet validated on device);
    they can adopt the same gate in a follow-up.
    
    With the overlap off (default), the main MoE path no longer issues any
    event records; with the overlap on, behavior is unchanged.
    
    ### Profiling
    
    Host-side timeline of one MoE layer step before and after this change:
    
    **Before (events recorded unconditionally on the routed stream):**
    
