    src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b41c554-8ee6-4c47-88e8-18b8053ca72e"
    />
    
    **After (records skipped when multistream overlap is off):**
    
    <img width="680" height="162" alt="image"
    src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d77d873f-6409-4d3d-b819-c311417668f2"
    />
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. With `multistream_overlap_shared_expert` enabled the behavior is
    unchanged; with it disabled only the unused event records are skipped.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - The runner-contract unit tests (`tests/ut/ops/test_fused_moe.py`)
    patch the overlap flag explicitly to keep exercising the record path,
    and new cases cover the skip path (milestones stay `None` with
    `record_event` never called); all other MoE tests (including 310P and
    LoRA) run unchanged.
    - CPU UT / pre-commit / DCO checks on this PR.
    - E2E MoE serving on Ascend NPU with `multistream_overlap_shared_expert`
    off (skip path) and on (unchanged path), plus the profiling screenshots
    above.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
